From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:35:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 49/66] ucode: decode SO_TIMESTAMPNS on musl

ucode-mod-socket maps SO_TIMESTAMPNS_OLD to SO_TIMESTAMP when the libc
does not define it, as musl does, so its control message table had two
entries for SO_TIMESTAMP and none for SO_TIMESTAMPNS: a nanosecond
receive timestamp reached the script as raw octets (B74). Backport the
upstream fix 2e0b25a2 as 015.

Bump PKG_RELEASE.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christopher Griffin <christophergriffin05@gmail.com>
---
 package/utils/ucode/Makefile                  |  2 +-
 ...-to-SO_TIMESTAMPNS-for-the-OLD-alias.patch | 32 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 33 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/utils/ucode/patches/015-socket-fall-back-to-SO_TIMESTAMPNS-for-the-OLD-alias.patch

diff --git a/package/utils/ucode/Makefile b/package/utils/ucode/Makefile
index 4fe6cc8600..b7315eff76 100644
--- a/package/utils/ucode/Makefile
+++ b/package/utils/ucode/Makefile
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=ucode
-PKG_RELEASE:=4
+PKG_RELEASE:=5
 
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
 PKG_SOURCE_URL=https://github.com/ucode-lang/ucode.git
diff --git a/package/utils/ucode/patches/015-socket-fall-back-to-SO_TIMESTAMPNS-for-the-OLD-alias.patch b/package/utils/ucode/patches/015-socket-fall-back-to-SO_TIMESTAMPNS-for-the-OLD-alias.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..53e3cc179a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/utils/ucode/patches/015-socket-fall-back-to-SO_TIMESTAMPNS-for-the-OLD-alias.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+From 2e0b25a23c0948caf54c0a9fdd3133922363c9d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
+Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 07:41:05 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] socket: fall back to SO_TIMESTAMPNS for the OLD alias
+
+A libc that does not define SO_TIMESTAMPNS_OLD, musl among them, took
+SO_TIMESTAMP instead, which is the microsecond option. The control message
+table then held two entries for SO_TIMESTAMP and none for SO_TIMESTAMPNS, so a
+nanosecond receive timestamp was never decoded and reached the script as raw
+octets.
+
+Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
+---
+ lib/socket.c | 2 +-
+ 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)
+
+diff --git a/lib/socket.c b/lib/socket.c
+index 44bb8566..0c316e9e 100644
+--- a/lib/socket.c
++++ b/lib/socket.c
+@@ -86,7 +86,7 @@
+ # endif
+ 
+ # ifndef SO_TIMESTAMPNS_OLD
+-#  define SO_TIMESTAMPNS_OLD SO_TIMESTAMP
++#  define SO_TIMESTAMPNS_OLD SO_TIMESTAMPNS
+ # endif
+ #endif
+ 
+-- 
+2.43.0
+
-- 
2.43.0

